  "id": "mental-accounting",
  "term": "mental accounting",
  "definition": "In this source, mental accounting refers to a cognitive approach to temporal decision-making in which people mentally organize time-related resources. It includes tendencies such as loss aversion, mental budgeting, and flexibility, and is linked to how people balance short-term and long-term rewards.",
